      "line": 1051,
      "text": "The IA-840f features three QSFP-DD ports. The QSFP-DD high speed interfaces are directly driven"
    },
    {
      "line": 1052,
      "text": "from IP within the user FPGA design. Intel provides IP cores for multiple high-speed protocols com-"
    },
    {
      "line": 1053,
      "text": "patible with the IA-840f which all have their own reference clock requirements. The IA-840f is populated"
    },
    {
      "line": 1054,
      "text": "with an on-board frequency clock device which, by default, feeds three independent 156.25 MHz (for"
    },
    {
      "line": 1055,
      "text": "100/40/10 GbE) to all three of the dedicated transceiver IP reference clock FPGA pins."
    },
    {
      "line": 1056,
      "text": "BittWare allocates 24 dedicated MAC addresses per IA-840f. These addresses are programmed in the"
    },
    {
      "line": 1057,
      "text": "ID PROM."
    },
    {
      "line": 1103,
      "text": ""
    },
