    },
    {
      "line": 1105,
      "text": "6.1.3 FPGA to QSFP Pin Mapping"
    },
    {
      "line": 1106,
      "text": "The twenty-four SerDes bidirectional lanes are connected to a single FPGA transceiver quad (9A). It is"
    },
    {
      "line": 1107,
      "text": "designed for up to 28Gbps NRZ. The traces are designed to meet the OIF CEI-28G-VSR specification"
    },
    {
      "line": 1108,
      "text": "requirements."
    },
    {
      "line": 1109,
      "text": "The Intel QSF constraints file is the point of reference for pin mappings; however, QSFP Pin Mapping"
